# Dart / Flutter build output and tooling state.
#
# A build directory must never be committed: it is machine-specific, it is
# regenerated by every `flutter build`, and it is large enough to make a diff
# unreviewable. `.build/` is here alongside `build/` because the Swift SDK repo
# (SwiftPM) uses that spelling, and the three SDK repos share this file's rules.
.dart_tool/
.packages
.pub-cache/
.pub/
build/
.build/
coverage/
doc/api/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Native build output from the plugins this SDK depends on. The example app's
# platform folders are ignored wholesale below, but these patterns are
# unanchored so they also catch a hand-made scratch project anywhere in the
# tree.
.gradle/
Pods/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.cxx/
local.properties

# `pubspec.lock` is deliberately NOT committed. This repo publishes a package
# (a library), not an application: a committed lock file would pin resolutions
# that consumers never use, and it would go stale against the version ranges in
# pubspec.yaml. The example app is a Flutter app but is checked out as part of
# this package, so it shares the rule.
pubspec.lock
example/pubspec.lock

# Generated platform folders in the example app. `flutter create .` regenerates
# them from `example/pubspec.yaml`; committing them means every Flutter upgrade
# shows up as an unreviewable diff. The two hand-written pieces the OAuth flow
# needs — the `<queries>` element and `LSApplicationQueriesSchemes` — are
# documented in `doc/oauth.md` so they can be re-applied after a regeneration.
#
# `example/android/` is the exception, and deliberately so. CI builds a real
# Android APK from it, which is the only step that proves the SDK's plugins
# link on a device; regenerating it meant CI built a project nobody had ever
# reviewed, and silently discarded the hand-edits the build needs. It is
# tracked instead, minus the parts the Flutter tool writes for itself — see
# `example/android/.gitignore`. A Flutter upgrade that changes that project is
# exactly the diff a maintainer should be reading.
example/ios/
example/linux/
example/macos/
example/windows/
example/web/
example/.flutter-plugins
example/.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# IDE and editor state.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
.vscode/
*.swp
.history/

# macOS.
.DS_Store

# Local overrides. `pubspec_overrides.yaml` is how a developer points this
# package at a local checkout of a dependency; that is a machine-local choice.
pubspec_overrides.yaml
.env
*.log
